WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.708 --> 00:00:09.107
Tom Lindqvist: Hey Darnell, good to hear your voice. How's Wednesday treating you down in Tampa?

2
00:00:09.568 --> 00:00:16.712
Darnell Wright: Hey Tom. Not bad. Busy week, we're prepping for the fall promo push, but I can't complain.

3
00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:24.605
Tom Lindqvist: Nice. I saw the call volume ticked up last week. You all holding up okay on staffing?

4
00:00:25.331 --> 00:00:37.868
Darnell Wright: Yeah, we're getting by. We had two folks out on PTO, so the queue got a little backed up Tuesday afternoon, but the team caught up by Wednesday morning.

5
00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:43.380
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. Anything you need from me on the routing side while you're shorthanded?

6
00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:57.046
Darnell Wright: Not right now. The Amazon Connect flows are doing their job. But I do want to flag something about the AI Voice Agent that's been nagging at us.

7
00:00:58.185 --> 00:00:58.985
Tom Lindqvist: Go ahead.

8
00:01:00.341 --> 00:01:10.288
Darnell Wright: So when the voice agent hands a call off to a live person, the stuff it already collected from the caller doesn't come through with the transfer.

9
00:01:10.288 --> 00:01:19.867
Darnell Wright: The caller tells the bot their order number, their name, what they need, and then my agent picks up and has to ask all over again.

10
00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:24.911
Tom Lindqvist: Does that happen on every transfer, or only certain call types?

11
00:01:25.302 --> 00:01:33.609
Darnell Wright: Seems like most of them. Store hours and order status calls that get escalated, the context just drops. And the callers notice.

12
00:01:33.609 --> 00:01:38.895
Darnell Wright: You can hear the frustration in their voice when they have to repeat themselves.

13
00:01:39.504 --> 00:01:42.544
Tom Lindqvist: How long has this been going on?

14
00:01:43.672 --> 00:01:53.632
Darnell Wright: A few weeks now. I didn't escalate it right away because we were in the middle of the showroom rollout for the new mattress line.

15
00:01:53.632 --> 00:01:56.421
Darnell Wright: But it's showing up in our numbers.

16
00:01:56.769 --> 00:01:57.569
Tom Lindqvist: Which numbers?

17
00:01:59.048 --> 00:02:07.891
Darnell Wright: CSAT on transferred calls is running lower than on the calls the AI handles end to end. Not a huge gap, but it's consistent.

18
00:02:07.891 --> 00:02:13.786
Darnell Wright: And my team is spending extra time on those calls because they're basically starting from scratch.

19
00:02:15.015 --> 00:02:23.632
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. I want to get this in front of the right folks. Do you have a recent call ID or two where it happened?

20
00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:27.956
Darnell Wright: I can pull a couple. I'll send them over after this call.

21
00:02:28.394 --> 00:02:35.226
Tom Lindqvist: Perfect. And is it affecting any specific showroom more than others, or is it across the board?

22
00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:41.568
Darnell Wright: Across the board, as far as I can tell. It's not tied to one location.

23
00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:53.077
Tom Lindqvist: Understood. I'll take this back to the product team and see what they need from us. I can't promise a timeline, but I'll keep you posted.

24
00:02:53.495 --> 00:02:56.031
Darnell Wright: That's all I ask. Appreciate it.

25
00:02:57.162 --> 00:03:01.674
Tom Lindqvist: Of course. Switching gears, how's the PreSense screen pop working for your agents?

26
00:03:02.123 --> 00:03:03.873
Darnell Wright: It's fine. No complaints there.

27
00:03:04.214 --> 00:03:08.907
Tom Lindqvist: Good. And the Google Ads and Meta conversions are still flowing?

28
00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:13.833
Darnell Wright: Yeah, no issues. My marketing counterpart checks them weekly.

29
00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:24.520
Tom Lindqvist: Great. One housekeeping thing: I'll be out the first week of October, so if anything urgent comes up, my teammate can step in.

30
00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.603
Tom Lindqvist: I'll send an intro email.

31
00:03:26.981 --> 00:03:29.359
Darnell Wright: Sounds good. I'll keep an eye out.

32
00:03:30.779 --> 00:03:37.813
Tom Lindqvist: Alright, I'll follow up once I hear back from the team. Thanks for the detail, Darnell.

33
00:03:38.026 --> 00:03:39.432
Darnell Wright: Thanks, Tom. Talk soon.
